{"dataset_id": "8a37cdf3-b540-4966-992c-4fe842d432bd", "created_at": 1795754003.802196, "expires_at": 1795757603.802196, "metadata": {"domain": "research", "query": "What happened between Verstappen and Hamilton at Turn 4 during the 2021 Brazilian GP?", "sources_count": 13, "grounded": 1}, "data": {"query": "What happened between Verstappen and Hamilton at Turn 4 during the 2021 Brazilian GP?", "summary": "During the **2021 S\u00e3o Paulo (Brazilian) Grand Prix** on **November 14, 2021**, a major title-contesting incident occurred between Max Verstappen (Red Bull) and Lewis Hamilton (Mercedes) on **Lap 48** at Turn 4 (Descida do Lago) [1.4, 1.5, 1.7]:\n\n### The Incident\nHaving closed the gap to Verstappen, Hamilton attempted an overtake around the outside of Turn 4 using DRS [1.3, 1.8]. Verstappen defended the inside line by braking extremely late [1.4, 1.7]. Verstappen's car understeered, running deep off the track limits onto the tarmac run-off area and forcing Hamilton's Mercedes wide as well to avoid a collision [1.4, 1.8]. No contact was made, and both drivers rejoined the track with Verstappen retaining the lead [1.4, 1.5].\n\n### The Stewards' Decision and Mercedes' Appeal\n* **In-Race Action**: The event was noted by FIA Race Control, but the stewards determined that **no investigation was necessary**, allowing the race to proceed without penalty [1.4, 1.8]. Hamilton later successfully overtook Verstappen on Lap 59 to win the race [1.4, 1.5].\n* **Right of Review**: On November 16, Mercedes requested a **\"Right of Review\"** under **Article 14.1.1 of the FIA International Sporting Code**, submitting newly released forward-facing onboard camera footage from Verstappen's car as new evidence [1.4, 1.11].\n* **Outcome**: On November 19, the stewards **denied** the review [1.2, 1.11]. They agreed the footage was new and relevant, but ruled it was not \"significant\" enough to overturn their decision or warrant a retrospective penalty [1.2, 1.7].\n\n### Driver Quotes\n* **Max Verstappen**: Defended his maneuvering as \"fair, hard racing,\" stating [1.7]: \n  > *\"We were fighting hard, braking late into the corner, the tyres were quite worn. If I would have turned more abrupt to the left, you'd just spin off the track... I thought it was a good battle.\"* [1.7]", "findings": ["* **In-Race Action**: The event was noted by FIA Race Control, but the stewards determined that **no investigation was necessary**, allowing the race to proceed without penalty [1.4, 1.8]. Hamilton later successfully overtook Verstappen on Lap 59 to win the race [1.4, 1.5].", "* **Right of Review**: On November 16, Mercedes requested a **\"Right of Review\"** under **Article 14.1.1 of the FIA International Sporting Code**, submitting newly released forward-facing onboard camera footage from Verstappen's car as new evidence [1.4, 1.11].", "* **Outcome**: On November 19, the stewards **denied** the review [1.2, 1.11]. They agreed the footage was new and relevant, but ruled it was not \"significant\" enough to overturn their decision or warrant a retrospective penalty [1.2, 1.7].", "* **Max Verstappen**: Defended his maneuvering as \"fair, hard racing,\" stating [1.7]:"], "sources": [{"title": "tntsports.co.uk", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH1Mp9wiOahx80JzqbFErwmfxpSWcyWs8tAGG4xp6rvbN1Rnv29vFQi7kp5Jyi8U3hlfq61IM-FfxxigvKJS0PpPjHrDO-kSDfV5R70U8xhdF_bEIwi5rK_LZ35KM8CkxoxXPGtYu9Aa_ynpuISqdFAQdH3XdoKeYgkrmj1VHk9etnu1IIRiJnb-VIxHQ38akc2eFc90WYR7l190-u_HNw9v_Fdfqa-M8001EQoThaCCYVi6DDevJzJWH-3uB5MQd-uxZXSsjKVkSwwvA4jtVF9PMIZSXhhwpktzuLqdkhNp16HALS9T1pvLfIR245d", "uri": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH1Mp9wiOahx80JzqbFErwmfxpSWcyWs8tAGG4xp6rvbN1Rnv29vFQi7kp5Jyi8U3hlfq61IM-FfxxigvKJS0PpPjHrDO-kSDfV5R70U8xhdF_bEIwi5rK_LZ35KM8CkxoxXPGtYu9Aa_ynpuISqdFAQdH3XdoKeYgkrmj1VHk9etnu1IIRiJnb-VIxHQ38akc2eFc90WYR7l190-u_HNw9v_Fdfqa-M8001EQoThaCCYVi6DDevJzJWH-3uB5MQd-uxZXSsjKVkSwwvA4jtVF9P